<Base title="Privacy Policy · Family Chores" description="Privacy policy for the Family Chores app by Beemik." accent="#6c5ce7">
  <section class="doc narrow">
    <div>
      <span class="eyebrow">Family Chores</span>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="updated">Last updated November 3, 2026</p>

      <p>Family Chores is made by Beemik and is built for families, including children. We keep it simple: we don't run servers, we don't have accounts, and we don't collect your family's information.</p>

      <h2>Information stored on your devices</h2>
      <p>Names, avatars, chores, points, coins and activity you enter stay on your family's own phones and tablets. We never receive them.</p>

      <h2>Home Wi-Fi sync</h2>
      <p>If you connect more than one device, they share data directly with each other over your home Wi-Fi network. Nothing is sent over the internet or to us.</p>

      <h2>Notifications</h2>
      <p>The app shows notifications on the device (for example, when a chore is traded). These are created on the device and are not sent through any outside service.</p>

      <h2>Ads</h2>
      <p>The app is free and shows ads from Google AdMob. All ad requests are marked as directed at children and limited to G-rated content, so ads are not personalized and are not based on your behavior. The app does not use the Android advertising ID. Google may collect limited device information, such as IP address, to show and measure ads and to prevent fraud. See <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites">how Google uses information from apps that use its services</a>.</p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>We do not knowingly collect personal information from children. The app is designed to be set up by a parent, and nothing a child enters leaves the family's devices except as described in the Ads section above.</p>

      <h2>Deleting your data</h2>
      <p>Uninstalling the app, or clearing its storage in Android settings, removes all of its data from that device.</p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>If this policy changes, we'll update this page and the date at the top.</p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions? Email <a href="mailto:support@beemik.com">support@beemik.com</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
